module Stryker
  class Instrumenter
    # A mutant that got no switch, and the reason, so that a run can report
    # the mutant with a status and say why.
    #
    # The reason is one of these:
    #
    # - `:no_switch_site`: no node around the mutant's site can hold a
    #   switch. That is the case inside `BEGIN { }`, which Ruby allows only at
    #   the top level of a file. It is also the case for a class or module
    #   name, and for a statement of a kind that no row of the placement
    #   table names, such as `@count = 0` or a `for` loop, at the top level of
    #   a file or directly in a class or module body, since neither a class
    #   nor a module holds a switch.
    # - `:no_one_line_form`: the mutant's text spans several lines, and
    #   refract's formatting of it has no form on one line, as a regexp with
    #   a line break inside it. A switch on several lines would move every
    #   line after it. It is also the reason when the plain mutant parses but
    #   has no one node in the parentheses where the mutant's text goes, as
    #   when the text starts with a line break, so there is no text to put on
    #   one line.
    # - `:does_not_parse`: the plain mutant, the original file with the
    #   source of the node that the switch wraps replaced by the mutant's text
    #   in parentheses, doesn't parse, so the mutant is not valid Ruby. A run
    #   reports it with the status `CompileError` of the shared report schema.
    #
    # A mutant with no switch site has no plain mutant, so its reason is
    # `:no_switch_site` whether or not its edit makes valid Ruby.
    #
    # A mutant that got no switch for either of the first two reasons is
    # reported with the status `Ignored` and a `status_reason` that says why,
    # so that no test can run with it, and it counts in no score.
    #
    # ## Examples
    #
    # ```ruby
    # skip = result.skipped.first
    # [skip.mutant.id, skip.reason]
    # # => [1, :no_switch_site]
    # ```
    class Skip < Data
      # The `status_reason` of each reason that gives the status `Ignored`.
      # Private.
      IGNORED: Hash[Symbol, String]

      # Why a mutant got no switch.
      type reason = :no_switch_site | :no_one_line_form | :does_not_parse

      # The mutant that got no switch.
      attr_reader mutant: Mutant

      # Why it got none.
      attr_reader reason: reason

      # The result of the mutant, which didn't run: `CompileError` for
      # `:does_not_parse`, and for each other reason `Ignored`, with a
      # `status_reason` that says why no test can run with the mutant.
      def result: () -> MutantResult

      # Builds the skip.
      #
      # - `mutant`: Stryker::Mutant, the mutant that got no switch.
      # - `reason`: Symbol, why it got none.
      def self.new: (mutant: Mutant, reason: reason) -> instance
                  | (Mutant mutant, reason reason) -> instance
    end
  end
end
